      ":question/id": "2a9c733a-3be1-55f9-ae18-d007236cde70",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-129050",
      ":question/problem": "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=6 \\\\ 9x+4y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y &=6 \\\\ 9x+4y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"
